--
N5008 [dcl.constexpr]/6 (constexpr declares the object const) and
[expr.const] (an element of a constexpr array, a member of a constexpr class
object built by a constexpr constructor, are constant expressions).
Non-vacuous: the last assertion is deliberately wrong and must FAIL.  Before
the fix the namespace-scope static_asserts were skipped -- silently; the
new "could not be evaluated" warning (forbidden above) is what exposed them.
